Fix PluginCLAP::activate() never reporting the plugin's initial latency

Generated against DPF commit 4238e1c7f0351bbe488d79f0899c540543ac7583
("Merge branch 'develop'", the commit pinned by AUDIOPLUGINS_DPF_GIT_TAG in
Hex/CMakeLists.txt). File: distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp.

WHAT IS BROKEN
--------------
The CLAP latency extension's contract (clap/ext/latency.h) is explicit:

    // Tell the host that the latency changed.
    // The latency is only allowed to change if the plugin is deactivated.
    // If the plugin is activated, call host->request_restart()
    // [main-thread]
    void (*changed)(const clap_host_t *host);

DPF's PluginCLAP::deactivate() honors this correctly -- it calls
checkForLatencyChanges(false, true) + reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded()
synchronously before returning, which is legal because the plugin is (about
to be) deactivated and deactivate() itself runs on the main thread.

PluginCLAP::activate(), the other place a plugin naturally first learns its
real latency (many plugins, including Hex, only know the sample rate --
and therefore their latency in samples -- once activate() provides it),
calls neither. Nothing reports the initial 0 -> real-latency transition
while still inside activate()'s call stack, where doing so directly would
be legal (the plugin isn't "activated" yet as far as the host's bookkeeping
about the *previous* latency value is concerned -- this is the standard
place essentially every other CLAP plugin wrapper reports first latency).

Instead, the first call to checkForLatencyChanges() only happens later, from
inside process()/flushParameters() (checkForLatencyChanges(true, false) at
the end of process(), or checkForLatencyChanges(active, !active) in
flushParameters()) -- by which point the plugin genuinely *is* active. Since
"active" is true there, DPF correctly avoids calling changed() directly
(per the spec, it isn't allowed to while active) and instead defers via
fLatencyChanged=true, reported later from onMainThread(). But that deferred
report itself still calls host->latency->changed() -- just now from outside
activate(), while the plugin is active, which is exactly the case the CLAP
spec says must use request_restart() instead. clap-validator's
transport-null/transport-fuzz/transport-fuzz-sample-accurate tests catch
this via their embedded clap_host_latency::changed hook, which asserts it
is only ever called from within clap_plugin::activate().

THE FIX
-------
Call checkForLatencyChanges(true, true) + reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded()
at the end of activate(), mirroring deactivate()'s existing two-line
pattern (isActive=true since we just activated; fromMainThread=true since
CLAP's activate() is main-thread-only, like deactivate()). This reports the
plugin's real initial latency synchronously, from within activate() itself,
which is legal per the spec and matches deactivate()'s already-correct
handling of the equivalent transition.

VERIFICATION
------------
clap-validator 0.4.1 against Hex.clap, before this patch (but with the
state-chunked-read patch from dpf-clap-state-chunked-read.patch already
applied): 44 tests run, 13 passed, 19 failed. All 19 failures were
transport-null/transport-fuzz/transport-fuzz-sample-accurate (repeated
across parametrized configurations), each failing with:

    clap_host_latency::changed
    Must only be called within 'clap_plugin::activate'

After this patch: those three tests all pass (verified by name, not just
count). 4 unrelated pre-existing failures remain (process-varying-sample-
rates producing `inf` at low sample rates, param-set-events/param-set-no-
cookies flush()-vs-process() mismatch on the output-only level parameters,
param-set-wrong-namespace not validating the event namespace ID) -- none
of those involve latency at all; they are separate, not-yet-investigated
issues tracked in Hex/CLAUDE.md, not caused or masked by this patch.

Not reported upstream yet -- that is a separate, deliberate decision, same
as dpf-clap-state-chunked-read.patch.

diff --git a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
--- a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
+++ b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
@@ -826,6 +826,10 @@ public:
         fPlugin.setSampleRate(sampleRate, true);
         fPlugin.setBufferSize(maxFramesCount, true);
         fPlugin.activate();
+       #if DISTRHO_PLUGIN_WANT_LATENCY
+        checkForLatencyChanges(true, true);
+        reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded();
+       #endif
     }

     void deactivate()
